## Re-attack #1: attempt-3's FAIL (real-name clobber) — FIXED, verified

The fix adds a name-compatibility guard to inferPositionalHealthcareLinks
(internal/services/retirement/settings.go): a pair links only if the
person's name is a placeholder OR normalizePersonName(person.Name) ==
normalizePersonName(hc.Name); the all-or-nothing per-pair loop already in
place now also fails the whole batch on any name mismatch.

$ go test ./internal/services/retirement/... -run 'TestPositionalHealthcareLinkInference_RealNameMismatchStaysUnlinked' -v
--- PASS: TestPositionalHealthcareLinkInference_RealNameMismatchStaysUnlinked (0.01s)
(persons "Robert"/"Susan", healthcare "Bob"/"Sue", exact age match — stays
unlinked, all four names/ages unchanged — this is literally last attempt's
regression fixture, now green.)

Mutation-kill (re-applied myself, m7): removed the name-compat guard block
from inferPositionalHealthcareLinks in the private copy —
$ go test ./internal/services/retirement/... -run 'TestPositionalHealthcareLinkInference_RealNameMismatchStaysUnlinked' -v
FAIL	budget2/internal/services/retirement	0.011s
Restored the file; `diff /tmp/settings.go.orig internal/services/retirement/settings.go` empty (private copy only — verified the real tree file was never touched by this: `diff /tmp/settings.go.orig <real-tree>/internal/services/retirement/settings.go` also empty).

