## Other attack surfaces re-checked (no new finding, per attempt-3 groundwork)
- Age-guard exact equality, twins/reordering inherent limitation, migration
  hard-fail-on-write-error blast radius (pre-existing on master 895d509,
  already flagged as backlog in attempt 3): unchanged this attempt, not
  re-litigated as FAIL grounds.
- normalizePersonName is case/whitespace-insensitive only (no nickname
  matching), so "Robert"/"Bob" correctly stay mismatched (m7); only true
  case/whitespace variants of the SAME name are treated compatible, and any
  cosmetic name-sync in that narrow case is the same ComputeAges
  person_id-linked sync behavior that already existed pre-CM1 for any
  explicitly person_id-linked entry (confirmed: prepare/normalize.go line 36,
  unchanged, not in this task's diff) — not a new regression.
- Double-empty-name positional match (both person.Name and hc.Name == ""):
  age-only linking possible, but no name is lost since both are already
  empty; unrealistic fixture shape, not the class of defect the claim
  addresses, and pre-existing linking-without-a-name-guard was already the
  behavior for this specific empty/empty shape before this fix (the guard
  only closes the REAL-name mismatch case). Reporting as backlog
  observation only, not a FAIL.

## Backlog observations (not FAIL grounds)
- Empty-name positional pairs (persons/healthcare both named "") can still
  link on age alone; harmless (nothing to lose) but arguably should be
  treated as name-incompatible too for defense in depth. Narrow, unlikely
  real-world fixture shape.
- (Carried from attempt 3, still true) migration-write-on-load hard failure
  in loadInternalContext is pre-existing master behavior and out of this
  task's writeable scope; CM1 attempt 4 actually REDUCES its blast radius
  (fewer plans now trigger `changed` on load), so this backlog item is
  smaller than it was at attempt 3, not larger.

## Conclusion
Both re-attacked findings (name clobber, no-write rule) are fixed with
mutation-killed permanent tests (m7, m8, m10 all reproduced RED on
reapplication). No load path writes without a real migration; no consumer
reads a stale on-disk date; use_current_month:false survives every save
path through the single saveInternal chokepoint. Oracle, build, vet, race,
gofmt all clean on the exact committed code (e80c679). PASS.
